        "id": 227489,
        "name": "QuirkyDM",
        "username": "QuirkyDM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-05-18T10:36:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Greazer and Haka went away first, like normal. I tried to take out Bugbear first but with Miss Information reducing damage, cards being destroyed so easily and him healing, it was not happening. So I took out Miss Information and beat up on everyone. With Fanatic able to use her base power at will thanks to the Seer and Argent Adept having multiple performances to play cards and use powers, I was often playing an extra 5-6 cards per round, which kept me ahead of the destruction going on and really let me dish out the damage. I was making a run for Bugbear, especially once Hallowed Halls came out and I could recycle Tempest's Lightning Strikes, and everything was well under control. Then I made my fatal error and didn't have Ermine destroy my top-decked End of Days. There went the entire set up. Bugbear still went down and the Operative went down once, but after that the heroes were at too low of health to withstand the onslaught.</p>\n<p>Second game did not involve the End of Days goof, and thus a Near Mint, though the final health totals were all low single digits.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:01:42.205Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
